## can the INCUMBENT exist on a 3.7 floor? (README open question 4)
#
# Asked with pip's own resolver against this container's configured index.
# Nothing is installed by this: it is a query, and the answer went the other
# way from the guess, which is why it is in a log rather than in prose.

   protobuf, newest wheel pip accepts per interpreter (manylinux2014_x86_64, cp):
     python 3.7   protobuf-4.24.4-cp37-abi3-manylinux2014_x86_64.whl
     python 3.10  protobuf-7.36.2-cp310-abi3-manylinux2014_x86_64.whl
     python 3.11  protobuf-7.36.2-cp310-abi3-manylinux2014_x86_64.whl
     python 3.13  protobuf-7.36.2-cp310-abi3-manylinux2014_x86_64.whl

   grpcio, newest wheel pip accepts per interpreter (manylinux2014_x86_64, cp):
     python 3.7   grpcio-1.62.3-cp37-cp37m-manylinux_2_17_x86_64.manylinux2014_x86_64.whl
     python 3.10  grpcio-1.84.0-cp310-cp310-manylinux2014_x86_64.manylinux_2_17_x86_64.whl
     python 3.11  grpcio-1.84.0-cp311-cp311-manylinux2014_x86_64.manylinux_2_17_x86_64.whl
     python 3.13  grpcio-1.84.0-cp313-cp313-manylinux2014_x86_64.manylinux_2_17_x86_64.whl

   So a 3.7 floor arm IS buildable, with an incumbent three years older than
   the target's. Under README R7 that makes any floor-against-target ratio a
   comparison of library versions as well as of runtimes, which is what
   README 5.2's arm b exists to avoid. Reported, not decided.

   Note for 9.2: protobuf's own wheel is cp3x-ABI3 and its upb extension on
   disk is _message.abi3.so. The incumbent already made the wheel-policy
   trade this slice is being asked to price.
